#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:953
#, no-c-format
msgid "Saving and retrieving your favourite playlists"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:954
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The disk icon (shown in the table above), at the bottom of your "
"<emphasis>Playlist pane</emphasis>, allows you to save the current &amarok; "
"playlist. This enables you to recall a particular selection of music from "
"your collection at any time. Playlists only contain pointers to the music "
"you selected, not the music itself. So if your playlist is pointing to music "
"on an external device, it must be connected and mounted, otherwise the music "
"cannot be played. There are three places to store playlists:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:957
#, no-c-format
msgid "outside &amarok; on your computer file system,"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:959
#, no-c-format
msgid "in your &amarok; playlist database"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:961
#, no-c-format
msgid "on an portable media device."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:964
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking the disk icon at the bottom of the <emphasis>Playlist pane</"
"emphasis> stores your playlist in the &amarok; playlist database. By "
"default, your saved playlist has a name composed of the date and time when "
"you saved it (see image below). By right-clicking the playlist name, you can "
"rename it to something more suitable. Right-clicking on a playlist name also "
"allows you to add it to your existing playlist in the <emphasis>Playlist "
"pane</emphasis>, or to replace your existing playlist."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:981
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Context View"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:982
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The power of &amarok; is in the <emphasis>Context pane</emphasis> (in the "
"center of the default &amarok; window), where you can install various "
"<emphasis>applets</emphasis> to help you enjoy and explore your music. Most "
"of this additional information is obtained from the Internet, so a "
"connection is important to get the most out of your <emphasis>Context pane</"
"emphasis>. By default, 3 <emphasis>applets</emphasis> are preset: "
"<emphasis>Current Track</emphasis>, <emphasis>Lyrics</emphasis> and "
"<emphasis>Wikipedia</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:984
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Default"
msgid "Default layout"
msgstr "លំនាំដើម​"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:985
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The default <emphasis>Context pane</emphasis> searches for the lyrics of the "
"song you are playing. If it finds the lyrics, it displays this in the bottom "
"half of the Context pane, while the top banner of the <emphasis>Context "
"pane</emphasis> displays the album cover and track information for the "
"current music. Sometimes lyrics are not available, because they may not be "
"stored in an appropriate resource on the Internet. In addition, the track "
"information for the current track needs to be <link linkend=\"tags\">tagged</"
"link> correctly for lyrics to be found. If lyrics are not found, this can be "
"due to various reasons, amongst them wrong informations in the Internet "
"sources like incorrect numbering system of the tracks within the album, and "
"the mis-representation of unusual text, such as when the title of a track "
"should contain characters with a circumflex, cedille or accent (ê,ç,à), but "
"does not."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1001
#, no-c-format
msgid "Customizing the Context pane"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1002
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At the bottom of the context pane are three buttons for the default applets. "
"On the right of these buttons you see a wrench, clicking on it will show a "
"red <guilabel>X</guilabel> allowing you to remove these applets. Click the "
"green <guilabel>+</guilabel> to add more display options (see image below). "
"Drag the labeled buttons to re-order the applets you have, and click the "
"wrench again to fix your selections. This makes the context pane extremely "
"flexible, maximizing the possibility of a custom display that fits your "
"preferences."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1019
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to deal with problems"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1020
#, no-c-format
msgid "Some of the music is being rapidly skipped over"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1021
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may not have installed the necessary <emphasis>codecs.</emphasis> More "
"about that here <ulink url=\"http://userbase.kde.org/Amarok/Manual/"
"FAQ#What_media_types_does_Amarok_support.3F\">FAQ: What Media Types Does "
"&amarok; Support</ulink>. Please refer to your distribution."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1024
#, no-c-format
msgid "After my iPod has been mounted, it is not shown in the Content Browser"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1025
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This should not happen. Check that the device has been properly mounted. "
"Simply typing <userinput>mount</userinput> in a console will show you all "
"mounted devices."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1028
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&amarok; cannot see the predefined playlists on my portable music player"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1029
#, no-c-format
msgid "Wait for the next version of &amarok;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1032
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After I have updated my collection, the additions are not shown in the "
"Content Browser"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1033
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Quit &amarok; from the <guilabel>Amarok</guilabel> menu, or use "
"<keycombo>&Ctrl;<keycap>Q</keycap></keycombo> to quit. Once you restart "
"&amarok;, your collection should show your updates."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1036
#, no-c-format
msgid "&amarok; cannot find the lyrics of the songs that I play"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1037
#, no-c-format
msgid "Possibilities:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1040
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The lyrics are not available in the sites checked on the Internet. You may "
"wish to add more sites via the script menu (<menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Script Manager</guimenuitem></menuchoice>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1042
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The track numbering system within an album in your collection is not correct."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1044
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The title of your song contains special characters with a cedille, accent, "
"&etc; that do not show in your track title. Therefore the lyrics script "
"applet cannot find a match for your title. Check your tags and track "
"numbering system with a tagger such as <ulink url=\"http://musicbrainz.org/"
"doc/MusicBrainz_Picard\">Picard</ulink>. Also see <ulink url=\"http://"
"userbase.kde.org/Special:mylanguage/Amarok/Manual/FAQ\">&amarok; FAQ</ulink>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1049
#, no-c-format
msgid "GLOSSARY"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1050
#, no-c-format
msgid "Breadcrumbs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1051
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is a way of navigating a hierarchical file structure; on &amarok; near "
"the top of the Media Sources pane. Starting at the Home folder level, it "
"shows how deep one has navigated into the file system. When you have gone to "
"a particular place in the file system, you will see all folders at a higher "
"level. In &amarok; the <guilabel>&gt;</guilabel> links between folder levels "
"allow you to find out what alternative folders are available at a particular "
"level. The breadcrumbs are an efficient mechanism to navigate the whole file "
"system on your computer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1054
#, no-c-format
msgid "Collection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1055
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All the sound files that &amarok; has compiled in the database. Your "
"collection may vary in size and composition of music tracks, depending which "
"external devices (such as audio &CD;s or portable players with music) are "
"connected and mounted on your computer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1058
#, no-c-format
msgid "Content Browser"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1059
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the central part of the <emphasis>Media Sources pane</emphasis> that "
"allows you to list the music that you have in your collection. The Content "
"browser allows you to select the sort order of your track lists as well as "
"the detail in which you wish to see your music."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1062
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Dynamic Playlists"
msgid "Playlist"
msgstr "បញ្ជី​ចាក់​ថាមវន្ត"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1063
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A selection of tracks from your collection that you wish to play. Some "
"portable music players have predefined playlists that are likely to differ "
"from your &amarok; playlists."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1066
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "script"
msgid "Script"
msgstr "ស្គ្រីប​"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1067
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&amarok; plugin to extend functionality. Scripts are available from "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Script Manager</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>. Add more lyrics sources, more streaming stations, "
"save covers to your album folders, burn &CD;s from playlists, &etc;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1070
#, no-c-format
msgid "Scrobble"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1071
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To scrobble a track means that as you listen to it, the title of the track "
"and artist are sent to a Web site such as Last.fm, where the information is "
"added to your profile."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1074
#, no-c-format
msgid "Stream, streaming"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1075
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Like 20th-century radio stations, Internet radio stations send out "
"<quote>streams</quote> of content. One can find music, news, commentary and "
"opinion. Many streams can be accessed through &amarok;, either through "
"scripts such as Cool Streams, or individually added by menu "
"(<menuchoice><guimenu>Playlist</guimenu><guimenuitem>Add Stream</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1078
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tags"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1079
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The information about each of the tracks you listen to, &eg; album name, "
"track title, composer, artist, year, &etc; There is a standard called ID3 "
"for including this information on audio &CD;s. You can edit the tags of "
"individual tracks within &amarok; if the file permissions are correct."
msgstr ""

